TEXT -360 -160 Left 2 ;pure ohmic load
TEXT -560 -112 Left 2 ;The generator has a fixed speed of (1500 turns/min)\nand is connected to a isolated network with no voltage source\nThe field voltage is 600V (more only at startup)\nThe load is increased from 2s on from 0 to 50MW\nThe voltage v1 decrease if the load increase\nWith this model you can plot the voltage v1 with the x-axis\nset to v(i1)
TEXT -224 -488 Left 2 ;General:\n \nThis model is a synchrongenerator without transformer, switch or regulator for speed or voltage\nThe speed is fix at (n_Turbine=1500)\nThe field voltage is set by a external PWL-source\n \nparams:\n            UN_verkettet=20000 Nominal voltage\n            IN=14.434k Nominal current\n            Pel=400e6 Nominal power (UN_verkettet*IN*cosphi of 0.8)\n            Kc=0.5 short-circuit ratio\n            UE0=600V Nominal field voltage\n            IE0=2000A Nominal field current\n            p=2 Number of poles      \n            Schenkelpolfactor=0.5 for salient pole machine (kc=0.8-1.0)\n                                              1 for cylindrical pole machine(kc=0.4-0.5)                               \n             Daempferfaktor=1 (damping factor)\n             Streuung=0.05 (leakage factor)\n             rcu=0.01 (rel. Copper resistance)\n             rbg=0.001 (rel. friction moment)\n             J=100000 (inertia)\n             a=0.9 parameter for nonlinear saturation\n             m=7  parameter for nonlinear saturation\n             n1=1500 The beginning speed\n             err0=0 (if err0=1 generator starts with full voltage!, because of spike set transient starting time to 1ms)\n             t_anlauf=2m Starting time\n             t_auslauf=2s Stopping time\n             t_betrieb=100s In-operation time\n             n_Turbine=Nominal speed turbine\n              \n \nAlternative elements: (changed via doubleclick on the Spicemodelline)\n          \nHINT: The power output can be computed with M*314.159/2  (P=M*omega/p)\n                    The load angle can be outputed with V(u1:u1:theta) \n                    The here constant frequency is n/30    2*n/60 = p*n/60 (p=Polcount)\n \nLibfile: Sgen.lib
TEXT -848 -96 Left 2 ;Since the generator acts here with fixed voltage (600V-field voltage)\nthere is no need for voltage regulation\nThe excitation voltage can be altered by means of a pwl source
TEXT -568 -264 Left 2 ;Switcher for assymetric\nload test
TEXT -808 -528 Left 2 ;At 3sec the phase 3 is opened with now makes a assymetric current system. \nThis system can be translated to a positive sequence, negative sequence and\nzero sequence system. The negative sequence system (-omega) has double velocity\nin relation to the rotor and induces alternating currents with double frequncy in the exciter \ncircuit. This alternating field can now also be divided into two rotating fields one with +omega\nand one with -omega. The field with +omega compensates the conterclockwise stator field above and\nthe other has now 3*omega related to the rotor and induces now stator currents with\nthree times the frequency of the net. You can see this with Edit/FFT (zoom before) especially if you set\nthe damping facotor of the generator to a very small value.\nInstead of asymetric load you can alternatively  try to short the third phase with a ground symbol.
RECTANGLE Normal 208 -64 -240 -512 2
